        <mxCell id="header-sub" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#e2e8f0&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;What happens between a player pressing Play in the launcher and the server knowing their progression.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;Scope: Arffornia_Launcher_V.5.2@215a845 (msAuthManager.js, minecraftManager.js), msmc 5.0.5, Velocity config in Provisioning@235d0b8, Arffornia_Mods@a72e114 (Arffornia.onPlayerJoin) · derived from code, 2026-10-29&lt;br&gt;First login shown; with a saved refresh token msmc refreshes instead of opening the Microsoft window. Java, NeoForge and mod sync are collapsed into one note (view content-delivery).&lt;br&gt;Inferred, not in Arffornia code: the client&amp;#39;s session join and Velocity&amp;#39;s hasJoined (standard online-mode protocol, onlineMode: true in infra proxy values). The ensure-exists call goes out to the public IP and back through the router to Envoy (G3); the router hop of that hairpin is not drawn.&lt;br&gt;v0.1 · source: architecture/arffornia/views/player-login.yaml&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#94a3b8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="74" width="3082" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
